WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.880
For the better part of two decades,
school improvement has been focused on

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.930
narrowing achievement gaps by boosting
the performance of low-achieving

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:17.880
students in reading and math. This
mission has undeniable merit, but it also

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:22.770
carries real costs. One cost is a lack of
attention to those students who are

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:26.640
hungry for learning that stretches
beyond the corners of state academic

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.860
standards. Another is that teachers feel
so obliged to focus on gap-closing

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.120
instruction that they feel far less
free to devote time and energy

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.870
to supporting advanced learning. When
students seek to master advanced math,

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:45.030
research historical essays, or plunge
into biochemistry, that should be

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:49.979
celebrated, not merely tolerated. As
William Fitzhugh, the founder of the

00:00:49.979 --> 00:00:53.940
world's only journal for academic
research papers by high school students,

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:58.229
has pointedly put it: "We could at least
encourage the crazy ones."

00:00:58.229 --> 00:01:03.359
So for 2019, here's a healthy resolution
for school improvement: Let's at least

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:07.680
make sure we're also encouraging the
passionate ones. How do you think schools

00:01:08.540 --> 00:01:09.800
How do you think schools

00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:14.159
can better support passionate students?
Let us know in our poll. Also, let us know

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:18.149
what other topics you'd like our
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be

00:01:18.149 --> 00:01:24.859
sure to like and subscribe for more
research and videos from AEI.

